# Cloudflare Pages security + cache headers for the public status site
# (status.driftstack.dev).
#
# Audit context: docs/internal/2026-05-20-csp-header-audit.md closed the
# security-header gap on customer-dashboard / admin-panel and confirmed
# marketing-site / docs already had headers — but it did NOT cover the
# status site, which shipped with NO security headers. This file closes
# that omission so the status surface matches the other four Astro Pages
# apps (all use X-Frame-Options: DENY + nosniff + Referrer-Policy).
#
# Cloudflare Pages copies public/_headers verbatim into the deploy and
# applies these per-path; first match wins, so specific patterns precede
# the /* catch-all. Format reference:
#   https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# ── Hashed Astro bundles + CSS ───────────────────────────────────────
# Astro emits hashed filenames under /_astro/* — content-stable for the
# lifetime of a deploy, so cache them forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Static media ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ── Security headers — applies to every path ─────────────────────────
# Mirrors the customer-dashboard posture (the strictest sibling). The
# status page is public + read-only with one interactive element (the
# incident-email subscribe form), so the threat is clickjacking that
# subscribe/unsubscribe control + MIME-sniffing of the served assets.
#   X-Frame-Options DENY: the page must not be embeddable in an iframe,
#     defeating clickjack overlays. (If embeddable status widgets are
#     ever wanted, relax to SAMEORIGIN or a CSP frame-ancestors allow-
#     list — a deliberate founder decision, not a default.)
#   X-Content-Type-Options nosniff: browsers must honour the declared
#     content-type (the SVG marks could otherwise be re-interpreted).
#   Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin: don't leak the full
#     status URL to outbound destinations.
#   Permissions-Policy: deny browser device/payment APIs the status page
#     never uses (defense-in-depth, matches dashboard/admin).
# No Cache-Control on /* (HTML stays default-fresh so incident updates
# propagate fast); CSP is deliberately deferred, same as the dashboard
# (Astro is:inline blocks need enumeration first — see the audit doc).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
